# E31 -- What draws a feature (water) population entry when nothing is fishing it? E26 left this loose end: the mussel entry fell 5005 to 4701 across a year on a fort with no fishing labour at load, and nothing in the tool touched it. This watches every stocked feature entry on LAKE for a full year with the tool COMPLETELY disabled — no roster, no water job — sampling the pool every 3,000 ticks. A steady drain says something consumes the pool continuously; steps say discrete events; no movement says E26's reading needs re-examining. Two replicates.
run 20260918-182837 fort LAKE backup LAKE.preverify
DF v0.53.16 win64 STEAM DFHack 53.16-r1.1 world The Domain of Winds site 48 tiles 12..13,28..28 seed 424242
commits: DwarfCron 835fddb seasonal-wildlife 41bbd19 fps cap 1000

## Predictions (written before the run)
- a continuous drain: the feature pool total falls steadily across the year, roughly linearly, with no obvious events
- discrete events: the total holds flat then steps down, so something specific consumes it and the step size names the consumer
- no drain at all: the pool is flat and E26's fall came from something the tool itself did

